@page "/not-found"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@*
  Page not found (T233; T335, flow 01: R2-NotFound-In, R2-NotFound-Out, R2-NotFound-Narrow; the round-2 review, S3 and
  S4; DESIGN.md § System pages). A browser's 404 is rerun here with its status kept (NotFoundPages), and the router shows
  it for an address no page claims inside a circuit.

  - It echoes no address: a crafted link would put its own words on a Wombat page (T285's class), and the address bar
    already shows it (S4).
  - It says nothing about records elsewhere: another institution's record is answered 404 so that it is not known to
    exist, and a sentence saying so would undo that (S4).
  - Signed out, the only way here is typing /not-found, since an unknown address sends a visitor to sign in first (S3).
*@
<PageTitle>Page not found · Wombat</PageTitle>

<AuthorizeView Context="notFoundAuth">
  <Authorized>
    <PageHeader Title="Page not found" Icon="search" />
    <div class="system-panel">
      <p>There is no page at this address.</p>
      <p class="muted">Check the address, or start again from Home.</p>
      <div class="actions-cell">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/"><Icon Name="home" />Go to Home</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Authorized>
  <NotAuthorized>
    <div class="system-card-page">
      <div class="system-card">
        <PageHeader Title="Page not found" Icon="search" />
        <p>There is no page at this address.</p>
        <div class="actions-cell">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/">Go to Home</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </NotAuthorized>
</AuthorizeView>
